{"id": "EUVD-2026-80441", "enisaUuid": "9681503c-8296-31d6-b0d2-59d5cb9d6f77", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: only redirty pinned folios in redirty_blocks\n\nredirty_blocks() pins folios with read_cache_folio() and then walks the\nsame range again with filemap_lock_folio() to redirty them and drop the\nreferences it took.\n\nCommit 5951fee46bef (\"f2fs: Use a folio in redirty_blocks()\") changed\nthe second pass to a do/while loop. If read_cache_folio() fails before\nanything is pinned, page_idx does not advance but the cleanup loop still\nruns once.\n\nIf readahead has already populated the failed folio in page cache, that\nextra iteration finds it and folio_put_refs(folio, 2) drops one\nreference too many. Later drop_caches or reclaim can then report\n\"BUG: Bad page state\".\n\nOnly redirty the range that was pinned successfully.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:34", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/445e4a1e6025ecd5312e9a95c1b234192c976ca1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89c65ec3c18903de763cf567c96ab3ef60e5f3b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85171332742e741ccd6f401c69b6e0d698119e72"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9c6f-r39g-mhg4", "CVE-2026-89841"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c321b96-f0d4-31dd-a0b8-d280277c5d53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "6eee72c7-0f12-31ea-a911-79c2f0527214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5951fee46befbf6176c86482432f4f76e522f16c <89c65ec3c18903de763cf567c96ab3ef60e5f3b0"}, {"id": "910cad0e-8472-3c07-8025-442b02effa1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "b7bba765-05c8-32db-a547-c53e91f87ad5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bd18c75a-6e9e-3f0c-846e-f920193db7be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "c0880da7-6c2f-3498-a03f-0d2d58eaa71e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5951fee46befbf6176c86482432f4f76e522f16c <445e4a1e6025ecd5312e9a95c1b234192c976ca1"}, {"id": "c2bff0f7-bd2f-3901-b2b1-a215bffe80fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5951fee46befbf6176c86482432f4f76e522f16c <85171332742e741ccd6f401c69b6e0d698119e72"}, {"id": "fb6b2d3c-6c48-3fa2-b78d-2c7aff31584d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "398704c5-4bf9-34c1-8b8e-0dde4cf36f5b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}